From: ub438a2920a8af647 at groups.google.com (Ajay Kumar)
Date: Sat, 25 Jan 2020 10:58:25 +0000
Subject: MAGIC design
Message-ID: <51H2NN5CDtk.pu0eF6rFEQAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl2-disc/c/51H2NN5CDtk/m/pu0eF6rFEQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi I have three different recipient parents crossed with one donor parent separately. I have ~100 RILs from each of these three crosses. Can I use R/qtl2 for this design? what should be the cross design?

From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Sat Jan 25 14:08:40 2020
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Sat, 25 Jan 2020 14:08:40 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl2-disc] MAGIC design
Message-ID: <51H2NN5CDtk.3fUgEgzQEQAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <51H2NN5CDtk.pu0eF6rFEQAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <51H2NN5CDtk.pu0eF6rFEQAJ@rqtl2-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl2-disc/c/51H2NN5CDtk/m/3fUgEgzQEQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I would view this as a NAM population, rather than MAGIC. They would need to be treated as three separate two-way RIL, with cross type "riself". R/qtl2 doesn't currently have the functionality for a combined analysis of three crosses.

karl

